  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 205 PM MDT WED SEP 23 2026\nTemperatures of near to around 5 degrees below normal will \npersist through the long-term period. Sunday will warm a few \ndegrees compared to Saturday, as our area gets a brief period of\nsouthwesterly return flow ahead of the next system. Consensus \nis still good on another cold front, weaker than that of Friday,\ncrossing over our area come late Sunday. This front will help \nkeep breezy west/northwest winds and the cool conditions in \nplace. This trough should keep the tropical moisture from \nactivity in the eastern Pacific south and east of our area. \nHowever, guidance has trended a little wetter with this front, \nsupporting a 15-30% chance of showers primarily across higher \nterrain of southwest Idaho. Although uncertainty is still on the\nhigher side in regard to moisture availability. Shortwave \nridging behind this trough will for dry conditions and a warming\ntrend into mid-week next week.",
